  "text_pages": [
    "Dong-A University Office Of  External International  Affairs > Dormitory\n스킵네비게이션\n본문바로가기\n주메뉴바로가기\nInternational Student Support\nDONG-A UNIVERSITY, WHERE WE MAKE YOUR HISTORY\n메인으로 이동\nInternational Student Support\nOffice of International Affairs\nAdmission\nGlobal Network\nInternational Relations Programs\nInternational Student Support\nBulletin Boards\n닫기\nDormitory\nDormitory\nInsurance\nVISA Information\nOther University Life\n닫기\nInternational Student Support\nInternational Student Support\nDormitory\nInsurance\nVISA Information\nOther University Life\nDormitory\nSNS 목록열기\nFACEBOOK 공유하기\nTWITTER 공유하기\nBLOG 공유하기\nSNS 목록닫기\n인쇄\nurl 복사\nSeokdang Global House\nSeokdang Global House is a dormitory exclusively built for international students studying at Dong-A University, established on July 1, 2015, with the aim of providing a comfortable living environment for international students.\nSeokdang Global House website\nDormitory information\n기숙사 정보 표 정보제공\nDivision\nSeokdang Global House\nLocation\nNear Dong-A University Bumin Campus\nSize\n7 floors to 15 floors, double occupancy rooms (2 students per room)\nFacilities\n92 rooms, maximum capacity of 184 people\nCost\nApproximately 850,000 won per semester (for a 4-month period)\nKey Facilities\nLaundry room, lounge, cafeteria.\nIncluded in Each Room\nBathroom, single bed, desk, chair, drawers, shoe rack, LAN cable, telephone.\nHanrim Dormitory\nHanlim Dormitory, which opened its doors in 2002, is a modern facility that can accommodate up to 1,046 students. It offers a comfortable living environment with double occupancy rooms. Each student room is equipped with a personal desk, chair, bookshelf, bed, shoe rack, wardrobe, hanger, telephone, and LAN connection. In addition, each room's private bathroom is equipped with a toilet, sink, and shower. On each floor, there are shared bathrooms, washrooms, and lounges. In the basement, you'll find additional facilities including a dining area, study rooms, an internet cafe, a fitness center, meeting rooms, laundry, and ironing rooms. These facilities are designed to provide a pleasant and comfortable university life\nHanrim Dormitory website\n한림생활관 표 정보제공\nDivision\nHanlim Dormitory (Seunghak Hall)\nLocation\nWithin Dong-A University Seunghak Campus\nSize\nBasement 1 floor, Ground 5 floors\nFacilities\n510 rooms (30 rooms for guest and students with disabilities) with a total capacity of 1,019 people\nCost\nApproximately 600,000 won per semester (for a 4-month period).s\nKey Facilities\nCafeteria, study rooms, internet cafe, fitness center, meeting rooms, lounge, laundry, and ironing rooms, etc\nIncluded in Each Room\nSingle bed, desk, chair, drawers (including a mirror and shoe rack), LAN cable, telephone"
  ],
